     ddrraawweerr..lluuaa — bootloader menu/screen drawer module

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ddrraawweerr..lluuaa contains functionality for drawing and manipulating the menu,
     logo, and brand to the screen.

     Before using the functionality provided by ddrraawweerr..lluuaa, it must be in‐
     cluded with a statement such as the following:

           local drawer = require("drawer")

   BBRRAANNDD DDEEFFIINNIITTIIOONNSS
     Brand definitions describe a “brand”, traditionally drawn above the menu.
     The exact position may be controlled by using the loader.conf(5) vari‐
     ables _l_o_a_d_e_r___b_r_a_n_d___x and _l_o_a_d_e_r___b_r_a_n_d___y.  The following keys may be de‐
     fined for a brand definition:

           ggrraapphhiicc  A table of strings containing rows of text to be drawn to
                    the screen.

   LLOOGGOO DDEEFFIINNIITTIIOONNSS
     Logo definitions describe a “logo”, traditionally to the right of the
     menu.  The exact position may be controlled by using the loader.conf(5)
     variables _l_o_a_d_e_r___l_o_g_o___x and _l_o_a_d_e_r___l_o_g_o___y.  The following keys may be de‐
     fined for a logo definition:

           rreeqquuiirreess__ccoolloorr  A boolean describing whether or not this logo defi‐
                           nition requires color.  If it is chosen to be drawn
                           and it requires color on a color-disabled boot,
                           ddrraawweerr..lluuaa will elect to use the default “orbbw”
                           logo rather than the chosen logo.

           ggrraapphhiicc         A table of strings containing rows of text to be
                           drawn to the screen.

           sshhiifftt           A table describing the _x and _y shift that should be
                           applied to all elements should this logo be se‐
                           lected.  This is typically used for shifting the
                           menu and brand if an empty or minimal logo are se‐
                           lected.

   CCUUSSTTOOMM BBRRAANNDDSS AANNDD LLOOGGOOSS
     The brand and logo system is designed to allow brands and logos to be
     easily plugged in.  When an unrecognized loader_brand or loader_logo are
     encountered, ddrraawweerr..lluuaa will attempt to include _b_r_a_n_d_-_$_{_l_o_a_d_e_r___b_r_a_n_d_}_._l_u_a
     or _l_o_g_o_-_$_{_l_o_a_d_e_r___l_o_g_o_}_._l_u_a respectively.  These files are expected to
     call either ddrraawweerr..aaddddBBrraanndd() or ddrraawweerr..aaddddLLooggoo() to add the requested
     branddef or logodef.  ddrraawweerr..lluuaa will attempt to do another lookup for
     the requested brand or logo before falling back to one of the following:

           ddrraawweerr..ddeeffaauulltt__bbrraanndd          The default brand to be used if the
                                         requested brand cannot be located.

           ddrraawweerr..ddeeffaauulltt__ccoolloorr__llooggooddeeff  The default logodef to be used if an
                                         invalid logodef is requested and
                                         loader(8) has been configured to al‐
                                         low output of color.

           ddrraawweerr..ddeeffaauulltt__bbww__llooggooddeeff     The default logodef to be used if ei‐
                                         ther an invalid logodef has been re‐
                                         quested, or a logodef has been re‐
                                         quested that requires color and
                                         loader(8) has been configured to not
                                         output color.

   FFRRAAMMEE SSTTYYLLEESS
     ddrraawweerr..lluuaa contains the definitions for the different frame styles that
     may be drawn around the menu.  Frame styles define the characters drawn
     for horizontal lines, vertical aligns, and each of the four corner
     styles.  The following keys may be defined for a frame style:

     •• horizontal

     •• vertical

     •• top_left

     •• bottom_left

     •• top_right

     •• bottom_right
     Frame styles are currently defined in the table ddrraawweerr..ffrraammee__ssttyylleess in‐
     dexed by the name used for loader_menu_frame.  No API currently exists
     for manipulating this table indirectly.

